apture-workers/multivariable/14033856/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd291374fc3a2db811fb749ce133827deed4896481da6f960a62a8004b6dfa39"} {"question" "q-72399" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72399" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "30"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "42"] ["math" "84"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72399" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "30"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{i}{j}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{i}{j} & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{i}{j}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(\\frac{1}{j}+\\frac{2}{j}+\\frac{3}{j}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}\\frac{6}{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}\\frac{6}{j} & =\\frac{6}{1}+\\frac{6}{2}+\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =6+3+2 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd291374fc3a2db811fb749ce133827deed4896481da6f960a62a8004b6dfa39"} {"question" "q-72398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}(1j+2j+3j) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}(j+2j+3j) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}6j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}6j & =6\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6+12 \\\\  & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd291374fc3a2db811fb749ce133827deed4896481da6f960a62a8004b6dfa39"} {"question" "q-72094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "22"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(i+j)^{2}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(i+j)^{2} & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(i+j)^{2}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}((1+j)^{2}+(2+j)^{2}+(3+j)^{2}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}((1+j)^{2}+(2+j)^{2}+(3+j)^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}((1+j)^{2}+(2+j)^{2}+(3+j)^{2}) & =((1+1)^{2}+(2+1)^{2}+(3+1)^{2})+((1+2)^{2}+(2+2)^{2}+(3+2)^{2}) \\\\  & =(4+9+16)+(9+16+25) \\\\  & =79\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd291374fc3a2db811fb749ce133827deed4896481da6f960a62a8004b6dfa39"} {"question" "q-72397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "20"] ["math" "25"] ["math" "29"] ["math" "50"] ["math" "79"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-72397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "79"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}5({a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}{a}_{ij}=220,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}{b}_{ij}=200.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying these rules to the given sum, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}5({a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & =5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}({a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) \\\\  & =5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}{a}_{ij}-5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{40}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 220-5\\cdot 200 \\\\  & =1,100-1,000 \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd291374fc3a2db811fb749ce133827deed4896481da6f960a62a8004b6dfa39"} {"question" "q-149656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "100"] ["math" "110"] ["math" "120"] ["math" "130"] ["math" "90"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "100"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149676" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-2)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{a}_{ij}=300,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{b}_{ij}=250.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149676" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-2) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{b}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}2 \\\\  & =300+250-(2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}1) \\\\  & =550-2({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1=mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}550-2({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}1) & =550-2\\cdot (15\\cdot 16) \\\\  & =550-480 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-2)=70.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149676" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd291374fc3a2db811fb749ce133827deed4896481da6f960a62a8004b6dfa39"} {"question" "q-149676" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149676" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "60"] ["math" "65"] ["math" "70"] ["math" "75"] ["math" "80"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149676" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "70"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}(1+{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{a}_{ij}=20,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{b}_{ij}=10.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}(1+{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}1+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}1)+20-10 \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}1)+10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1=mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}1)+10 & =10\\cdot 12+10 \\\\  & =120+10 \\\\  & =130.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}(1+{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})=130.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd291374fc3a2db811fb749ce133827deed4896481da6f960a62a8004b6dfa39"} {"question" "q-149661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "120"] ["math" "130"] ["math" "140"] ["math" "150"] ["math" "160"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "130"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1-{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}=10,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij}=20.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1-{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)-10-20 \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)-30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1=mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)-30 & =5\\cdot 10-30 \\\\  & =50-30 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1-{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})=20.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd291374fc3a2db811fb749ce133827deed4896481da6f960a62a8004b6dfa39"} {"question" "q-149603" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149603" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-20"] ["math" "-25"] ["math" "-29"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "25"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149603" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}(3{a}_{ij}+4{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}{a}_{ij}=50,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}{b}_{ij}=55.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying these rules to the given sum, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}(3{a}_{ij}+4{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}3{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}4{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}{a}_{ij}+4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{70}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 50+4\\cdot 55 \\\\  & =150+220 \\\\  & =370.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd291374fc3a2db811fb749ce133827deed4896481da6f960a62a8004b6dfa39"} {"question" "q-149658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "340"] ["math" "350"] ["math" "360"] ["math" "370"] ["math" "380"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "370"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}5{b}_{j}({a}_{i}-4)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i}=85,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{j}=18.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}5{b}_{j}({a}_{i}-4) & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}5{b}_{j}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}({a}_{i}-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}5{b}_{j}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}({a}_{i}-4) & =(5{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{j})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}4) \\\\  & =(5{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{j})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i}-4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}1) \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 18)\\cdot (85-4\\cdot 20) \\\\  & =(90)\\cdot (85-80) \\\\  & =(90)\\cdot (5) \\\\  & =450\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd291374fc3a2db811fb749ce133827deed4896481da6f960a62a8004b6dfa39"} {"question" "q-149726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "450"] ["math" "550"] ["math" "580"] ["math" "650"] ["math" "685"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "450"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{i}({b}_{j}-5)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i}=25,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{j}=58.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{i}({b}_{j}-5) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}({b}_{j}-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}({b}_{j}-5) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{j}-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}5) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{j}-5{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1) \\\\  & =(25)\\cdot (58-5\\cdot 10) \\\\  & =(25)\\cdot (58-50) \\\\  & =(25)\\cdot (8) \\\\  & =200\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd291374fc3a2db811fb749ce133827deed4896481da6f960a62a8004b6dfa39"} {"question" "q-149689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "150"] ["math" "200"] ["math" "250"] ["math" "280"] ["math" "300"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "200"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({a}_{i}+1)({b}_{j}-1)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{a}_{i}=20,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{j}=26.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({a}_{i}+1)({b}_{j}-1) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}({a}_{i}+1){\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({b}_{j}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}({a}_{i}+1){\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({b}_{j}-1) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{a}_{i}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{j}-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}1) \\\\  & =(20+5)\\cdot (26-20) \\\\  & =(25)\\cdot (6) \\\\  & =150.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149717" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd291374fc3a2db811fb749ce133827deed4896481da6f960a62a8004b6dfa39"} {"question" "q-149717" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149717" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "140"] ["math" "150"] ["math" "160"] ["math" "180"] ["math" "200"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149717" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "150"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{a}_{i}({b}_{j}-6)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i}=15,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{b}_{j}=68.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{a}_{i}({b}_{j}-6) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}({b}_{j}-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}({b}_{j}-6) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{b}_{j}-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}6) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{b}_{j}-6{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}1) \\\\  & =(15)\\cdot (68-6\\cdot 11) \\\\  & =(15)\\cdot (68-66) \\\\  & =(15)\\cdot (2) \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149742" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd291374fc3a2db811fb749ce133827deed4896481da6f960a62a8004b6dfa39"} {"question" "q-149742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "28"] ["math" "30"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "40"] ["math" "42"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149742" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "30"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}+3)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}=35,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}{b}_{j}=20.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}+3) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({b}_{j}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({b}_{j}+3) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}2)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}3) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}{b}_{j}+3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}1) \\\\  & =(35-2\\cdot 15)\\cdot (20+3\\cdot 15) \\\\  & =(35-30)\\cdot (20+45) \\\\  & =(5)\\cdot (65) \\\\  & =325.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bd291374fc3a2db811fb749ce133827deed4896481da6f960a62a8004b6dfa39"} {"question" "q-149736" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149736" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "325"] ["math" "335"] ["math" "352"] ["math" "353"] ["math" "355"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "q-149736" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "325"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/state.json" "file_sha256" "3b92bf7c2e0a7336db5b69780453e95bb404f3f571d250ab3dbc67da28086241"} {"question" "e-6116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^3\\sum_{i=1}^2 (i+j).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/example-6116.json" "file_sha256" "86be565e80c2745031ce76f7930c50bf7c76ade99af468a498e891c433af0f3c"} {"question" "e-6116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(i+j) & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(i+j)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}[(1+j)+(2+j)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(3+2j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the sum above by summing over the index $j\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(3+2j) & =(3+2\\cdot 1)+(3+2\\cdot 2)+(3+2\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =5+7+9 \\\\  & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/example-6116.json" "file_sha256" "86be565e80c2745031ce76f7930c50bf7c76ade99af468a498e891c433af0f3c"} {"question" "e-6118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8}  a_{ij} = 8, \\qquad\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8}  b_{ij} = 15.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/example-6118.json" "file_sha256" "c451e3fc255b878131b263913b485eda09ecf65e661d6ab671fe5bbd7c045db9"} {"question" "e-6118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}(1+2{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}2{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+2(8)-15 \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n 1 = mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+1 & =5\\cdot 8+1 \\\\  & =40+1 \\\\  & =41.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij}) = 41.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/example-6118.json" "file_sha256" "c451e3fc255b878131b263913b485eda09ecf65e661d6ab671fe5bbd7c045db9"} {"question" "e-10521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15} \\sum_{j=1}^{18} (a_{i} - 2)( b_{j}+1)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15}a_i = 40, \\qquad \\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^{18}b_j =-8 .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/example-10521.json" "file_sha256" "54da10fd0e068ec6f85b0c4e7a486a6a402c050ce3d03956c7343e098ea61106"} {"question" "e-10521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n  a_{i}b_j = \\sum_{i=1}^m a_i \\sum_{j=1}^n b_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}+1) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({b}_{j}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({b}_{j}+1) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}2)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}1) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}1) \\\\  & =(40-2\\cdot 15)\\cdot (-8+18) \\\\  & =(10)\\cdot (10) \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033856/example-10521.json" "file_sha256" "54da10fd0e068ec6f85b0c4e7a486a6a402c050ce3d03956c7343e098ea61106"}] "usage" {"q-72094" [] "e-10521" [] "e-6118" [] "e-6116" [] "q-149603" []} "basis" 1425 "retractions" [[17592186129787 :question/problem "What is $∑_(j = 1)^(2)∑_(i = 1)^(3)ij$?"] [17592186129435 :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nFind the value of the double sum\n\n$∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(10)(1 - a_{ij} - b_{ij})$\n\ngiven that\n\n$∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(10)a_{ij} = 10, ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(10)b_{ij} = 20$."] [17592186128927 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^3\\sum_{i=1}^2 (i+j)$."] [17592186128927 :question/worked-solution "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(j = 1)^(3)∑_(i = 1)^(2)(i + j) &= ∑_(j = 1)^(3)[∑_(i = 1)^(2)(i + j)] \\\\\n&= ∑_(j = 1)^(3)[(1 + j) + (2 + j)] \\\\\n&= ∑_(j = 1)^(3)(3 + 2j)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the sum above by summing over the index $j$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(j = 1)^(3)(3 + 2j) &= (3 + 2 \\cdot 1) + (3 + 2 \\cdot 2) + (3 + 2 \\cdot 3) \\\\\n&= 5 + 7 + 9 \\\\\n&= 21\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128928 :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij})$\n\ngiven that\n\n$\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} a_{ij} = 8, \\qquad\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} b_{ij} = 15$."] [17592186128928 :question/worked-solution "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)(a_{ij} + b_{ij}) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)a_{ij} + ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)b_{ij}, \\\\\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)ka_{ij} &= k∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)a_{ij}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)(1 + 2a_{ij} - b_{ij}) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1 + ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)2a_{ij} - ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)b_{ij} \\\\\n&= (∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1) + 2∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)a_{ij} - ∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)b_{ij} \\\\\n&= (∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1) + 2(8) - 15 \\\\\n&= (∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1) + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n 1 = mn\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(∑_(i = 1)^(5)∑_(j = 1)^(8)1) + 1 &= 5 \\cdot 8 + 1 \\\\\n&= 40 + 1 \\\\\n&= 41\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij}) = 41\n$$"] [17592186128770 :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15} \\sum_{j=1}^{18} (a_{i} - 2)(b_{j}+1)$\n\ngiven that\n\n$\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15}a_i = 40, \\qquad \\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^{18}b_j =-8$."] [17592186128770 :question/worked-solution "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n a_{i}b_j = \\sum_{i=1}^m a_i \\sum_{j=1}^n b_{j}\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(15)∑_(j = 1)^(18)(a_{i} - 2)(b_{j} + 1) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(15)(a_{i} - 2)∑_(j = 1)^(18)(b_{j} + 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(15)(a_{i} - 2)∑_(j = 1)^(18)(b_{j} + 1) &= (∑_(i = 1)^(15)a_{i} - ∑_(i = 1)^(15)2) \\cdot (∑_(j = 1)^(18)b_{j} + ∑_(j = 1)^(18)1) \\\\\n&= (∑_(i = 1)^(15)a_{i} - 2∑_(i = 1)^(15)1) \\cdot (∑_(j = 1)^(18)b_{j} + ∑_(j = 1)^(18)1) \\\\\n&= (40 - 2 \\cdot 15) \\cdot (-8 + 18) \\\\\n&= (10) \\cdot (10) \\\\\n&= 100\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186126417 17592186126418 17592186126419 17592186126420 17592186126421 17592186128517 17592186128518 17592186128519 17592186128520 17592186128521] "immutable_fields" [[17592186126416 :answer-field/correct] [17592186126416 :answer-field/id] [17592186126416 :answer-field/key] [17592186126416 :answer-field/type] [17592186128516 :answer-field/correct] [17592186128516 :answer-field/id] [17592186128516 :answer-field/key] [17592186128516 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
